  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 217 PM CDT Mon Aug 10 2026\n\nFor the rest of the day, pleasant conditions will prevail \nacross the Northland under mostly sunny skies. Elevated wildfire\nsmoke drifting overhead may cause hazy skies at times. As we \nhead into tonight, cloud cover will gradually increase across \nthe region. A weak passing disturbance will bring a slight \nchance of rain showers and isolated storms after midnight (no\nsevere weather expected). However, precipitation probability \nfor tonight is capped at thirty percent as incoming moisture \nbattles dry air in place over the area, resulting in little to \nno accumulation.\n\nOn Tuesday, mostly sunny skies will return for much of the day\nwith only a lingering slight chance of morning showers. Weather\ndisturbances diving through the persistent northwest flow aloft\nwill bring another chance for showers and non-severe storms\nTuesday night. Recent guidance indicates that showers and storms\nTuesday night into Wednesday have taken a more southerly track.\nUncertainty in the placement of convection, shower and\nthunderstorm chances for Tuesday night are also capped at \nthirty percent. Furthermore, as these weak features continue to \nbattle the ambient dry airmass over our region, very little \nrainfall accumulation is expected.\n\nHeading into Wednesday, partly sunny conditions are expected to\nprevail. With the bulk of the upper-level energy shifting south of\nthe Northland, only scattered rain showers and a slight chance of\nafternoon thunderstorms remain in the forecast. High pressure will\nthen build into the Upper Midwest for Thursday, providing quiet,\ndrier weather and mostly clear to partly cloudy skies across the\nentire area.\n\nLooking toward the end of the week, comfortable mid-August\nweather will continue on Friday with partly sunny skies. A\nstronger low-pressure system is forecast to approach the area\nFriday night into Saturday, bringing a more widespread chance\nfor rain showers and embedded thunderstorms. Cloud cover will\nincrease Friday night with rain chances peaking on Saturday.\nAs the system moves east Saturday night, precipitation will\ntaper off, leading to partly sunny skies on Sunday.",
